WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.302
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:05.204
You're here! You made it!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.204 --> 00:00:08.441
Wow. What a crowd.

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:09.909
Well, guys,
this is very exciting.

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:12.678 line:0%
Last night was the season
premiere of "The Bachelorette."

00:00:12.678 --> 00:00:14.614 line:0%
[ Woman cheers ]
Yeah.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:17.617
I'm pumped for this season
'cause we get to see people

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:19.351
spreading viruses
the old-fashioned way.

00:00:19.351 --> 00:00:21.754
You know?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:23.990
That's right.
After a year locked inside,

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:26.425
viewers were like, "You know,
hooking up with 30 strangers

00:00:26.425 --> 00:00:28.661
doesn't seem so crazy anymore."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:32.331
That's right. "The Bachelorette"
is back and everyone's fired up.

00:00:32.331 --> 00:00:34.300
But you just got to remember
it's a staged show

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.003
that's mostly fake,
kind of like a boxing match

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:38.637
between Floyd Mayweather
and Logan Paul.

00:00:38.637 --> 00:00:39.839
So just know that.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:45.411
[ Cheers and applause ]
Know it going in.

00:00:45.411 --> 00:00:46.879
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:50.416
♪ -Are we done forever? ♪
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:51.817
-You see this?

00:00:51.817 --> 00:00:54.120
At one point they introduced
a contestant named Connor B.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.055
with a short video,
and it's pretty interesting.

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:57.924
Well, you tell me if you think
it's interesting. Watch.

00:00:57.924 --> 00:01:04.597 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:05.931 line:0%
-I'm Connor B.

00:01:05.931 --> 00:01:08.568 line:0%
I am 29 years old, and I'm
from Nashville, Tennessee.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:12.138
Eighth graders,
I'm going to miss you guys!

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:14.440
My main occupation
is a math teacher.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:19.546
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:21.281
-Wait, what?

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:23.049
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:24.550
-After that bath video,

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.819
I think it's safe to say
he "was" a math teacher.

00:01:26.819 --> 00:01:29.088
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my God.

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:30.989
-Yep, Connor might not
find love,

00:01:30.989 --> 00:01:33.158
but his substitute just found
a full-time job, so...

00:01:33.158 --> 00:01:38.464
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:42.034
[ Vocalizes ]

00:01:42.034 --> 00:01:45.438
-I'll play a ukulele
in a bathtub.

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:48.574
-Get this. Another contestant,
Cody, listed his job --

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:51.044 line:0%
check this out --
as zipper sales manager.

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:52.946 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:55.949
Wait, a zipper salesman
and he's single?

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:58.251
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.251 --> 00:02:00.019
-Lots of ups and downs
on that job, you know?

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:01.087
-What's that?

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:02.554
-A lot of ups and downs
on that job.

00:02:02.554 --> 00:02:04.023
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:11.330
[ Rimshot ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:13.132
-If that wasn't strange enough,

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:16.636 line:0%
another contestant said that he
was a surgical skin salesmen.

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:18.737 line:0%
[ Audience ohs ]

00:02:18.737 --> 00:02:20.572
'Cause if there's one thing
women love to hear

00:02:20.572 --> 00:02:23.610
on a first date, it's, "Well,
I sell human skin. Hiya."

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:24.944
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:26.479
That's right.
"The Bachelorette" is back,

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:27.780
and even though
it was the first episode,

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.348
things got pretty intense.

00:02:29.348 --> 00:02:31.584
The emotions on that show
can be a little hard to handle

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:33.052
sometimes,
so I thought we could help.

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:34.386
Here's a clip from the episode

00:02:34.386 --> 00:02:38.257
re-voiced with the least
emotional person we know, Siri.

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:40.993
This is "Let's Get Siri-ous."

00:02:40.993 --> 00:02:42.394
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:42.394 --> 00:02:44.964
-Let's get Siri-ous.

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:46.432
-I don't like you, bro.

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:48.067
Like, I've never liked you
and that's fine.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.502
We don't have to talk at all,
bro.

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:52.438
Right. Right. And it's not
my fault I don't like you, bro.

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:55.441
You know, bro, you don't like
me, so that is your fault.

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.877
I'm like, "What are you
talking about, dude?"

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:59.945
I'm literally just telling you
exactly what's up, bro.

00:02:59.945 --> 00:03:01.414
That's it.
Alright, man.

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:03.616
I don't agree with anything
that you said,

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:05.551
but okay, that's fine, man.
Bro.

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:07.486
I don't think there was a need
for that at all, bro.

00:03:07.486 --> 00:03:08.754
Ha, ha, ha, ha.

00:03:08.754 --> 00:03:11.925
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:13.526
-What?

00:03:16.929 --> 00:03:20.132
And in more "Bachelor" news,
today ABC announced

00:03:20.132 --> 00:03:22.768 line:0%
that Chris Harrison is
officially exiting the franchise

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:24.770 line:0%
after 19 years.
[ Audience awws ]

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:27.073
Yep, Harrison knew there was
trouble when the producers

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:28.474
brought his suitcase
to the meeting.

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:30.376
[ Laughter ]
"No, you're kidding."

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:32.845
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:35.047
It's going to be awkward in
the finale when the limo driver

00:03:35.047 --> 00:03:37.116
lowers the partition
to reveal it's Chris Harrison.

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:38.851
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.653
Right now he's editing
his résumé like,

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:43.255
"matchmaker with 19 years
experience

00:03:43.255 --> 00:03:46.392
and 3 successful couples?"

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:49.495
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:52.665
"Give or take."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:55.768
"Two successful couples?"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:59.538
Some political news --
Lester Holt sat down with

00:03:59.538 --> 00:04:02.508
Vice President Kamala Harris
for an exclusive interview.

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:05.445
And when he asked why she hasn't
visited the border yet,

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.713
you can tell that she didn't
quite have an answer prepared.

00:04:07.713 --> 00:04:08.915
Listen to this.

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:11.483
-Do you have any plans
to visit the border?

00:04:11.483 --> 00:04:14.420
-At some point.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:17.122
We are going to the border.
We've been to the border.

00:04:17.122 --> 00:04:20.525
So this whole thing
about the border,

00:04:20.525 --> 00:04:21.827
we've been to the border.

00:04:21.827 --> 00:04:24.764
We've been to the border.
-You haven't been to the border?

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:26.899
-And I haven't been to Europe.

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:32.805
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:34.741
-Well, that escalated quickly.

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:37.377
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:39.645
That's right.
Harris was not in the mood.

00:04:39.645 --> 00:04:41.314
Don't be surprised
if you see Lester Holt

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:43.216
narrating his own episode
of "Dateline."

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:44.583
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:46.352
"It started out
as a normal interview."

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:47.854
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:50.423
Meanwhile, it was just announced
that former President Trump is

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:53.225 line:0%
launching a speaking tour
with Bill O'Reilly...

00:04:53.225 --> 00:04:57.163 line:0%
[ Audience groans ]
...called "the history tour."

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:58.698
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:00.800
When he heard,
Sean Hannity was like,

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:04.504
"Well, I met someone new and
totally awesome too, so, um."

00:05:04.504 --> 00:05:07.973
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.973 --> 00:05:09.409
It should be a fun tour.

00:05:09.409 --> 00:05:11.410
Backstage passes automatically
come with

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:14.380
a hush money payment
of $130,000. Isn't that nice?

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.048
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:16.048 --> 00:05:20.086 line:0%
And I read that the CDC issued
a warning that salmonella

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:22.988 line:0%
has been linked to
some breaded chicken products.

00:05:22.988 --> 00:05:24.590
With chicken sandwiches
at stake,

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:27.527
even conspiracy theorists
were like, "Vaccines, now!"

00:05:27.527 --> 00:05:28.961
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:31.130
"Put the Bill Gates in me!
Let's go!"

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:34.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.269
"I'm going to Popeyes!"

00:05:36.269 --> 00:05:38.771
[ Laughter and applause ]
"You're not stopping me!

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:41.908
I'm going to Popeyes!
Give me the 5G!"

00:05:41.908 --> 00:05:45.411
[ Applause ]

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:47.413
Some fashion news --

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:51.516
Balenciaga just unveiled
its new stiletto Crocs.

00:05:51.516 --> 00:05:52.952
Here's a photo.

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:57.156
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:59.058
It's a great way
to be comfortable

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:00.760
and uncomfortable
at the same time.

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:01.894
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:03.829
Yep, stiletto Crocs,

00:06:03.829 --> 00:06:05.865
or as strippers call them,
business casual.

00:06:05.865 --> 00:06:11.871
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:14.774
Give it up for your dancer,
Herman!

00:06:14.774 --> 00:06:17.977 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:17.977 --> 00:06:20.078
[ Air horn ]

00:06:20.078 --> 00:06:21.748
-Stiletto.

00:06:21.748 --> 00:06:24.617
-And finally, a pizzeria
in Rhode Island

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:27.519
just introduced a new employee.
Watch this.

00:06:27.519 --> 00:06:30.422
-A robot named Servi is
now attending to customers

00:06:30.422 --> 00:06:32.057
at Angelo's Palace Pizza.

00:06:32.057 --> 00:06:34.527
So far, she's been a big hit,
with many customers

00:06:34.527 --> 00:06:37.029
requesting a table
in Servi's section.

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:40.499
She can chat with guests and
even wish them a happy birthday.

00:06:40.499 --> 00:06:41.734
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:44.070
And just like a real server,
Servi waits until

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.271
the exact moment you take
a huge bite before asking,

00:06:46.271 --> 00:06:48.307
"How's everything tasting
over here?"

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:49.741
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.741 --> 00:06:51.844
Yep, it's a great innovation,
especially when

00:06:51.844 --> 00:06:54.447
the last customer leaves
and Servi becomes Moppy.

00:06:54.447 --> 00:06:56.415
[ Laughter and applause ]
We have a great show, everyone!

00:06:56.415 --> 00:06:58.050
Give it up for the Roots!

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:06.091 line:0%
♪♪

00:07:06.091 --> 00:07:14.133 line:0%
♪♪

00:07:14.133 --> 00:07:16.635
What a show we have for you
tonight.

00:07:16.635 --> 00:07:18.537
Thank you.
This is a perfect crowd.

00:07:18.537 --> 00:07:20.172
-This is perfect!
-This is perfection!

00:07:20.172 --> 00:07:24.477
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:24.477 --> 00:07:28.514
Joining us in studio, his new
movie "In the Heights" premieres

00:07:28.514 --> 00:07:32.618
this Thursday --
Lin-Manuel Miranda is here!

00:07:32.618 --> 00:07:33.819
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:33.819 --> 00:07:35.621
Oh, yeah!
Getting a standing ovation.

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:37.456
No, he's not here yet.
No, don't stand up.

00:07:37.456 --> 00:07:38.790
-No, later.
-He's not coming out.

00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:39.692
Later he'll come out.

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:40.959
-He's not hiding
behind the chair.

00:07:40.959 --> 00:07:42.662
-Got a standing ovation
just saying his name.

00:07:42.662 --> 00:07:45.364
[ Cheers and applause ]
I love that.

00:07:45.364 --> 00:07:47.633
Plus, from the Netflix series
"Bridgerton,"

00:07:47.633 --> 00:07:49.368
Phoebe Dynevor is here!

00:07:49.368 --> 00:07:53.272
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:53.272 --> 00:07:55.741
And you want to talk about
two cool kids right here?

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:58.743
We have music from Sharon
Van Etten and Angel Olsen.

00:07:58.743 --> 00:08:00.212
Come on, look at that!

00:08:00.212 --> 00:08:04.950
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:07.285
Guys, it's hard to believe,
but it's been over a year

00:08:07.285 --> 00:08:09.088
since we all got on Zoom,

00:08:09.088 --> 00:08:12.024
and yet some people are
still getting the hang of it,

00:08:12.024 --> 00:08:13.793
even people on TV,
so you know what that means.

00:08:13.793 --> 00:08:15.294
It's time for
another installment of

00:08:15.294 --> 00:08:17.729
"Greatest Moments
in Zoom History."

00:08:17.729 --> 00:08:18.797
Enjoy.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:18.797 --> 00:08:22.268 line:0%
♪♪

00:08:22.268 --> 00:08:23.835
-What do you think is
most important,

00:08:23.835 --> 00:08:25.705
most urgent right now?

00:08:27.273 --> 00:08:29.775
[ Laughter ]

00:08:31.243 --> 00:08:37.249
-We also heard reports that
grant funding has gone down de--

00:08:37.249 --> 00:08:38.651
[ Laughter ]

00:08:38.651 --> 00:08:40.285
-I think I lost
Representative Clark.

00:08:40.285 --> 00:08:43.455
-I understand that
Congresswoman Clark is back on.

00:08:43.455 --> 00:08:46.091
-I hope this is
a more successful outing.

00:08:46.091 --> 00:08:47.293
We are s--

00:08:47.293 --> 00:08:49.061
[ Laughter ]

00:08:49.061 --> 00:08:50.896
-I love them both.
I hope it's true.

00:08:50.896 --> 00:08:52.899
That would be awesome.
-Oh! Very good. Alright.

00:08:52.899 --> 00:08:54.333
-We were just saying
the same thing.

00:08:54.333 --> 00:08:56.302
Oh, no!
[ Laughter ]

00:08:56.302 --> 00:08:58.403
-Representative Gerry Connolly
of Virginia,

00:08:58.403 --> 00:09:02.074
who's the president of the NATO
Parliamentary Assembly,

00:09:02.074 --> 00:09:03.709
for five minutes.

00:09:03.709 --> 00:09:06.745
-[ Indiscernible robotic voice ]

00:09:06.745 --> 00:09:09.214
-I'm having a hard time
hearing you, Mr. Connolly.

00:09:09.214 --> 00:09:11.150
You're coming in --

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:15.888
You're breaking up.
It's hard to understand you.

00:09:15.888 --> 00:09:17.455
-[ Robotic voice ]
Can you hear me now?

00:09:17.455 --> 00:09:18.858
[ Laughter and applause ]

